gives rise to a bilinear ‘inner product’ V ×V → F . This inner product can
be regarded as an ‘internal’ version of duality. The natural action of GL( V )
induces a ‘dual’ action on V ∗ which is diﬀerent from its action on V .
Similarly, an internal version of triality is given by the product on the
octonion algebra, or more precisely by the trilinear form O×O×O →F deﬁned
