Finally we describe the six ‘pariahs’ in Section 5.9: the remaining three
Janko groups J 1, J 3 and J 4, and the simple groups of O’Nan (O’N), Rudvalis
(Ru) and Lyons (Ly). It should be noted that the only apparent relationship
between these groups is that J 1 is a subgroup of O’N. In particular, the three
